
== §1 — NO DESIGN, NO LOADS, NO CODE ==
  ✓ the structural spec names no structural code
  ✓ regulatory rule count is still zero
  ✓ real occupancy classification count is still zero
  ✓ browser spec is byte-identical to acs_struct.json
  ✓ ten structural element types declared
  ✓ DESIGNED / SAFE / COMPLIANT are not model statuses
  ✓ UNSAFE / DANGEROUS / CODE_VIOLATION are not severities
  ✓ rule is not a structural provenance value
  ✓ no compiled structural element carries a load, capacity or compliance field
  ✓ no compiled output uses structural-compliance language
  ✓ the language actually used is representational

== §2 — THE SYSTEM IS NEVER INFERRED FROM BUILDING TYPE ==
  ✓ a warehouse is not given steel just because it is a warehouse
  ✓ a warehouse column with no stated section keeps section=null
  ✓ a villa is concrete only because the fixture says so
  ✓ a model with no structural block produces no structural element
  ✓ and that model is still perfectly valid
  ✓ the compiler never invents a foundation to stand the 3D model on

== §3 — PROVENANCE AND STATUS ==
  ✓ every element records a provenance from the declared vocabulary
  ✓ a fixture-sourced model is not called verified data
  ✓ test_fixture is not in the verified-source list
  ✓ an undeclared status is derived, never assumed
  ✓ ai_inference is a distinct provenance from a verified one
  ✓ the model as a whole is never marked regulatory
  ✓ synthetic fixtures declare themselves synthetic

== §4 — GRID ==
  ✓ one grid system with six lines
  ✓ X and Z grids are both supported
  ✓ a grid line records whether its position was stated
  ✓ a grid system carries its own origin and rotation
  ✓ multiple grid systems per building are representable
  ✓ a rotated grid is not assumed to lie on the project world axes
  ✓ an unresolved grid reference is reported, not silently dropped
  ✓ a suggested grid is a SUGGESTION, never model truth
  ✓ every suggested line is sourced system_suggested, not user
  ✓ a suggestion is not written into the model
  ✓ no spacing supplied ⇒ no grid is invented
  ✓ no footprint ⇒ the suggestion refuses rather than guessing
  ✓ the suggestion says in writing that it is not design

== §5 — COLUMNS ==
  ✓ nine villa columns compile
  ✓ a column height comes from the architectural levels, not the renderer
  ✓ a column names the levels it spans
  ✓ a stated section is carried verbatim
  ✓ a column with no section keeps section=null
  ✓ and that is reported as INFO, never as an error
  ✓ structural_role stays unknown unless the model states it

== §6 — DISPLAY FALLBACK IS NEVER STRUCTURAL DATA ==
  ✓ an unknown section still yields render geometry
  ✓ but that geometry is labelled display_fallback
  ✓ and the semantic section stays null beside it
  ✓ every render item declares where its geometry came from
  ✓ the warehouse render items are all fallback-driven
  ✓ the villa render items are model-driven
  ✓ a fallback never appears in the rule inputs
  ✓ the spec states the fallback policy in writing
  ✓ compiling does not write the fallback back into the model

== §7 — BEAMS ==
  ✓ seven declared beams and not one auto-connected pair
  ✓ no beam was invented between neighbouring columns
  ✓ a beam resolves both endpoints to structural nodes
  ✓ beam length is measured, not assumed
  ✓ a beam naming a missing node is reported twice: bad ref and unresolved endpoint
  ✓ a beam given bare points is flagged floating, not silently accepted
  ✓ a zero-length beam is an ERROR

== §8 — STRUCTURAL SLAB / WALL / CORE ARE NOT THE ARCHITECTURAL ONES ==
  ✓ the architectural slabs are untouched by the structural layer
  ✓ a structural slab exists only where the model declares one
  ✓ a structural slab says it is a separate element
  ✓ an architectural wall is never reclassified as structural
  ✓ a shear wall role appears only because the fixture states it
  ✓ a wall with no stated role stays unknown
  ✓ an elevator shaft is not called a lateral core by itself
  ✓ a structural core spanning levels emits CORE_SPANS_LEVELS
  ✓ the architectural stair core is still its own element

== §9 — FOUNDATIONS ==
  ✓ nine isolated footings, exactly as declared
  ✓ no soil property is ever produced
  ✓ a foundation never claims a bearing capacity
  ✓ an unrecognised foundation type falls back to other, not to a guess
  ✓ a foundation with no supported member is reported
  ✓ a foundation naming a member that does not exist is an ERROR
  ✓ a foundation outside the site is reported factually
  ✓ the foundation type is never chosen from the building type

== §10 — MATERIALS ==
  ✓ a material label alone carries no strength
  ✓ no elastic modulus or density is inferred
  ✓ every optional property carries its own provenance
  ✓ a supplied property is kept with imported provenance
  ✓ the spec states that concrete implies no f′c
  ✓ an unknown material stays unknown
  ✓ a member with no material reference is reported as INFO
  ✓ a member naming a missing material is an ERROR

== §11 — NODES AND LEVEL ALIGNMENT ==
  ✓ nodes take their elevation from the architectural level table
  ✓ a node with an invalid level reference is reported
  ✓ no member floats on renderer-only coordinates
  ✓ the structural level table mirrors the architectural one

== §12 — COLUMN STACKING, OFFSET AND ALIGNMENT BREAK ==
  ✓ a column directly over another is aligned
  ✓ a 0.4 m shift is reported as an offset, not as aligned
  ✓ an offset is a WARNING and no transfer beam is designed
  ✓ a column with nothing under it is an alignment break, reported only
  ✓ no transfer element was added to the model by the break
  ✓ alignment states never leave the declared vocabulary
  ✓ a stack edge is confirmed only when actually aligned
  ✓ a three-storey stack aligns on every level

== §13 — RELATIONSHIPS ARE NOT LOAD PATHS ==
  ✓ every relationship type is in the declared vocabulary
  ✓ every relationship carries the not-a-load-path note
  ✓ a column touching a beam yields COLUMN_SUPPORTS with an explicit disclaimer
  ✓ no relationship says a member carries anything
  ✓ the spec states the rule in capitals
  ✓ a declared slab support is confirmed; an undeclared one is never invented
  ✓ a foundation placement relationship says no bearing check was made
  ✓ relationship ids are unique and namespaced

== §14 — STRUCTURAL ↔ ARCHITECTURAL INTERACTION ==
  ✓ a column standing in a door opening is reported
  ✓ a column inside a stair void is reported
  ✓ a column inside the elevator travel path is reported separately
  ✓ every clash states the basis it was tested on
  ✓ a beam along a wall carrying a door is INFO and says clearance is not evaluated
  ✓ a column inside a room is a spatial relationship, not a prohibition
  ✓ a column far outside the footprint is reported, not moved
  ✓ no clash is auto-fixed — the model is returned unchanged

== §15 — INTEGRITY VALIDATION ==
  ✓ the deliberately broken fixture triggers every integrity check
  ✓ every issue code is declared in the spec with a severity
  ✓ every issue carries a severity from the declared list
  ✓ issues are ordered ERROR first, then WARNING, then INFO
  ✓ no issue is a code-compliance verdict
  ✓ an unknown structural collection is reported and NOT interpreted
  ✓ a foreign building id is caught rather than silently re-namespaced

== §16 — DETERMINISM, NAMESPACING AND TRANSFORMS ==
  ✓ compiling twice gives byte-identical output
  ✓ the compiler never mutates the model it reads
  ✓ a second building namespaces every structural id
  ✓ two buildings can never collide on an id
  ✓ a transform never changes the compiled geometry
  ✓ the building transform is applied on read
  ✓ rotation is applied about the building origin
  ✓ grid lines respect the building transform too

== §17 — REVISION HASH ==
  ✓ moving a column changes the model hash
  ✓ removing a beam changes the model hash
  ✓ changing a section changes the model hash
  ✓ adding a foundation changes the model hash
  ✓ changing a material property changes the model hash
  ✓ toggling layer visibility does NOT change the model hash
  ✓ moving the camera still does not change the hash
  ✓ compiling the structure does not change the hash
  ✓ a model with no structural block hashes exactly as before

== §18 — RENDER AND EXPORT ==
  ✓ render items use the STRUCT| naming convention
  ✓ every structural kind that has geometry is represented
  ✓ render items never carry an engineering verdict
  ✓ a column render box sits between its two level elevations
  ✓ grid render items are lines, not boxes
  ✓ the structural layer is separate from the architectural layers
  ✓ colour distinguishes element kind only, never status

== §19 — RULE ENGINE CONTRACT (INPUTS ONLY) ==
  ✓ structural facts are exposed as future rule inputs
  ✓ a missing fact stays missing rather than defaulting
  ✓ no regulatory rule was added anywhere
